## 5. Where we stopped — important for tomorrow

We have not yet run the following command. It was the proposed next step:

Bash

```
sudo ovs-ofctl -O OpenFlow13 mod-port s4 v64b down
```

It temporarily disables the S4–S6 link to break the loop for the first connectivity test.

After running it, verify:

Bash

```
sudo ovs-ofctl -O OpenFlow13 show s4 | grep -E 'v64b|v47a|v34b'
sudo ovs-ofctl -O OpenFlow13 show s6 | grep v64a
```

Then retry:

Bash

```
sudo ip netns exec hostA ping -c 4 -W 2 10.200.0.2
```

If the ping still fails, stop and share the outputs. Don't add manual flows or change the controller yet. To restore the link if needed:

Bash

```
sudo ovs-ofctl -O OpenFlow13 mod-port s4 v64b up
```

Only do that if you need to restore the original topology; we can decide based on the test result.

## 6. What we will collect next

Once basic connectivity works, we can build a repeatable metrics-collection process.

